# The build context is the whole directory unless this excludes it. Without this file
# a local `data/` (1.5 GB of Parquet), `artifacts/` and the caches are shipped to the
# daemon on every build — slow, and it puts gitignored local data inside an image that
# gets scanned and pushed. Excluded rather than ignored: nothing in the image's build
# path reads any of it.
data/
datasets/
artifacts/
cache/
results/../cache
.venv/
.git/
.github/
docs/
ops/
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
models/
*.log
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.parquet
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/